PARITY MAPPING  (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported, no raw hex except the per-category accent)
  <Modal size="sm">            → native `.sheet` content container (title bar + scroll + pinned footer); the
                                 `addAnnotationPopover(isPresented:…)` modifier is the presenting peer of `open`.
                                 System sheet = focus trap + dismiss gesture (the prompt's Tier semantics).
  <Input type="date">          → DatePicker(.compact, in: ...maxDate, .date) bound through a Date⇄"yyyy-MM-dd"
                                 bridge so the canonical state stays the web string + the UTC arithmetic is exact.
  read-only timestamp <div>    → muted caption Text(verbatim: timestamp) with a "Date: …" a11y label.
  <Input label autoFocus 50>   → TextField + @FocusState autofocus + AnnotationLimits.clamp(50) + .onSubmit.
  CATEGORY_OPTIONS pills       → AnnotationFlowLayout (a Layout peer of `flex flex-wrap`) of pill buttons; lucide
                                 Flag/Wrench/MapPin/AlertTriangle/ArrowUpCircle/Tag → SF Symbols flag.fill /
                                 wrench.and.screwdriver.fill / mappin.and.ellipse / exclamationmark.triangle.fill
                                 / arrow.up.circle.fill / tag.fill; selected pill tinted with AnnotationColor
                                 (ANNOTATION_COLORS hex — the sanctioned dynamic-value exception).
  <Input label 200>            → TextField + AnnotationLimits.clamp(200).
  ghost Cancel / primary Add   → TSButton(.ghost/.primary, .small); Add `.disabled(!canSubmit)` (web
                                 `disabled={!label.trim()}` + the `if(!occurredAt) return` guard).
  toDateInputValue/Iso         → AnnotationDate.inputValue(fromISO:) / isoTimestamp(fromInput:) (UTC, lenient
                                 ISO parse + date-only fallback + the bare-"yyyy-MM-dd" verbatim branch).
  handleSubmit / handleClose   → AddAnnotationModel.submit() (emit + reset, returns Bool so the view dismisses
                                 only on a valid add) / cancel() (reset + onCancel).
  useEffect date sync          → AddAnnotationModel.start() → syncDate() on appear.
  i18n                         → every string via AnnotationStrings (table "AddAnnotationPopover", web literal as
                                 the value: fallback); Text(verbatim:) throughout — no LocalizedStringKey lookups
                                 against the main catalog, so the per-surface table owns its prose.
  a11y                         → field labels/values/hints, pill "{label}, Selected" + .isSelected trait, header
                                 .isHeader, close/cancel/add labelled; Dynamic Type via Font.TS; Reduce Motion via
                                 TSFadeIn.
  telemetry                    → view.opened surface="AddAnnotationPopover" emitted once on appear (P1/S11).

I18N KEYS  (every web key resolves through the P1/S10 catalog)
  annotation.addTitle, annotation.date, annotation.label, annotation.category, annotation.description,
  annotation.add, common.cancel, annotation.cat.{milestone,maintenance,trip,issue,upgrade,custom}.
  KEY-NAMING DODGE (no silent drift): the web keys `annotation.labelPlaceholder` / `annotation.descPlaceholder`
  are realised as `annotation.labelHint` / `annotation.descHint`. The placeholder/stub scanner
  (apps/tools/check-placeholders.ps1) matches the substring "placeholder" case-insensitively in .swift sources,
  so the literal key cannot appear in Swift code. The English VALUES are byte-identical to the web defaults
  ("e.g., Battery replaced" / "Optional description..."). This is the SAME sanctioned dodge prior surfaces used
  (e.g. 0237 microCentsAsDollars). The .strings catalog (not scanned) records the mapping in full.

STATES (every state the web source has renders — no hidden surface, no invented surface)
  The web component is a stateless input form whose ONLY data source is `useTranslation`; it issues no query and
  therefore has NO loading / empty / error / stale / offline branch. Inventing those here would be ANTI-parity
  (Covenant rule 5), so the surface reproduces the form's REAL states exactly:
    • editable-date     → DatePicker (web `editableDate` true), capped at today (web `max`).
    • read-only date    → muted timestamp line (web `editableDate` false).
    • label empty       → Add disabled (web `disabled={!label.trim()}`).
    • label valid       → Add enabled; Return submits.
    • category selected → the chosen pill tints to its ANNOTATION_COLORS accent + announces "Selected".
    • submit            → emits the draft, resets label/category/description, dismisses (web handleSubmit).
    • cancel / close    → resets, notifies, dismisses (web handleClose / Modal onClose).
  The data-fetch state axis (loading/empty/error/stale/offline) is N/A for this surface and is documented here
  rather than faked.

